### Bank Accounts API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for bank account management endpoints
### All operations for creating, reading, and managing bank accounts
### Reviewed and verified against implementation

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@bankAccountId = your-bank-account-uuid-here

### ============================================
### GET MY BANK ACCOUNTS
### ============================================
### Get all bank accounts for the authenticated user
### Requires user JWT token
### All sensitive data is automatically decrypted

GET {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Bank accounts fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "bank-account-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "beneficiaryName": "John Doe",
###       "iban": "SA0380000000608010167519",
###       "swift": "ALBISARI",
###       "addressLine1": "123 Main Street",
###       "addressLine2": "Building 5",
###       "city": "Riyadh",
###       "province": "Riyadh",
###       "country": "Saudi Arabia",
###       "postalCode": "12345",
###       "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### CREATE BANK ACCOUNT
### ============================================
### Create a new bank account for the authenticated user
### Requires user JWT token
### All sensitive data is automatically encrypted before saving

POST {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "beneficiaryName": "John Doe",
  "iban": "SA0380000000608010167519",
  "swift": "ALBISARI",
  "addressLine1": "123 Main Street",
  "addressLine2": "Building 5",
  "city": "Riyadh",
  "province": "Riyadh",
  "country": "Saudi Arabia",
  "postalCode": "12345"
}

### Request Body Fields:
### - beneficiaryName: Full name of account beneficiary (required, 1-255 chars)
### - iban: International Bank Account Number (required, 15-34 chars)
### - swift: SWIFT/BIC code (required, exactly 8 chars)
### - addressLine1: Primary address line (required, 1-255 chars)
### - addressLine2: Secondary address line (optional, max 255 chars)
### - city: City name (required, 1-100 chars)
### - province: Province/State name (required, 1-100 chars)
### - country: Country name (required, 2-100 chars)
### - postalCode: Postal/ZIP code (optional, max 20 chars)

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Bank account created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "bank-account-uuid",
###     "userId": "user-uuid",
###     "beneficiaryName": "John Doe",
###     "iban": "SA0380000000608010167519",
###     "swift": "ALBISARI",
###     "addressLine1": "123 Main Street",
###     "addressLine2": "Building 5",
###     "city": "Riyadh",
###     "province": "Riyadh",
###     "country": "Saudi Arabia",
###     "postalCode": "12345",
###     "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### Error Response (Missing Required Fields):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Validation error",
###   "errors": [
###     {
###       "field": "iban",
###       "message": "IBAN is required"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### Error Response (Invalid IBAN Length):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Validation error",
###   "errors": [
###     {
###       "field": "iban",
###       "message": "IBAN must be at least 15 characters"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### Error Response (Invalid SWIFT Length):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Validation error",
###   "errors": [
###     {
###       "field": "swift",
###       "message": "SWIFT code must be exactly 8 characters"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### CREATE BANK ACCOUNT (MINIMAL)
### ============================================
### Create a bank account without optional fields

POST {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "beneficiaryName": "Jane Smith",
  "iban": "SA0380000000608010167520",
  "swift": "ALBISARI",
  "addressLine1": "456 Second Street",
  "city": "Jeddah",
  "province": "Makkah",
  "country": "Saudi Arabia"
}

### Note: addressLine2 and postalCode are optional and will be null if not provided

### ============================================
### DELETE BANK ACCOUNT
### ============================================
### Delete a bank account by ID
### Requires user JWT token
### Users can only delete their own bank accounts

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts/{{bankAccountId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Example with actual UUID:
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Bank account deleted successfully"
### }

### Error Response (Not Found):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Bank account not found or you don't have permission to delete it"
### }

### Error Response (Invalid UUID):
### {
###   "success": false,
###   "message": "Validation error",
###   "errors": [
###     {
###       "field": "id",
###       "message": "id must be a valid UUID"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - All endpoints require user JWT token
###    - Users can only access their own bank accounts
###    - Include Authorization header: Authorization: Bearer <your-jwt-token>

### 2. ENCRYPTION & SECURITY
###    - All sensitive fields are automatically encrypted before saving to database
###    - Encrypted fields: beneficiaryName, iban, swift, addressLine1, addressLine2,
###      city, province, country, postalCode
###    - Data is automatically decrypted when retrieved from database
###    - Encryption uses AES-256-CBC algorithm
###    - Encryption key is stored in ENCRYPTION_KEY environment variable

### 3. VALIDATION RULES
###    - beneficiaryName: Required, 1-255 characters
###    - iban: Required, 15-34 characters (standard IBAN format)
###    - swift: Required, exactly 8 characters (SWIFT/BIC code format)
###    - addressLine1: Required, 1-255 characters
###    - addressLine2: Optional, max 255 characters
###    - city: Required, 1-100 characters
###    - province: Required, 1-100 characters
###    - country: Required, 2-100 characters
###    - postalCode: Optional, max 20 characters

### 4. ERROR RESPONSES
###    - 400 Bad Request: Validation errors (missing fields, invalid format, etc.)
###    - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid authentication token
###    - 404 Not Found: Bank account not found or user doesn't have permission
###    - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

### 5. DATA ISOLATION
###    - Users can only see and manage their own bank accounts
###    - Attempting to access another user's bank account returns 404
###    - Each bank account is tied to a specific userId

### 6. IBAN FORMAT
###    - IBAN (International Bank Account Number) must be 15-34 characters
###    - Format: Country code (2) + Check digits (2) + Bank identifier + Account number
###    - Example: SA0380000000608010167519 (Saudi Arabia)

### 7. SWIFT CODE FORMAT
###    - SWIFT/BIC code must be exactly 8 characters
###    - Format: Bank code (4) + Country code (2) + Location code (2)
###    - Example: ALBISARI (Al Rajhi Bank, Saudi Arabia)

### 8. USAGE EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Get All My Bank Accounts
GET {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Example 2: Create Bank Account with All Fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "beneficiaryName": "Ahmed Al-Saud",
  "iban": "SA0380000000608010167519",
  "swift": "ALBISARI",
  "addressLine1": "King Fahd Road",
  "addressLine2": "Tower A, Floor 10",
  "city": "Riyadh",
  "province": "Riyadh",
  "country": "Saudi Arabia",
  "postalCode": "11564"
}

### Example 3: Create Bank Account (Minimal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "beneficiaryName": "Mohammed Ali",
  "iban": "SA0380000000608010167520",
  "swift": "NCBKSAJE",
  "addressLine1": "Olaya Street",
  "city": "Riyadh",
  "province": "Riyadh",
  "country": "Saudi Arabia"
}

### Example 4: Delete Bank Account
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bank-accounts/{{bankAccountId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Keep bank account information up to date
###    - Verify IBAN and SWIFT codes before submitting
###    - Use proper address formatting
###    - Delete unused bank accounts to maintain security
###    - Never share your JWT token

### 10. SECURITY NOTES
###     - All sensitive data is encrypted at rest in the database
###     - Data is decrypted only when retrieved for authorized users
###     - Encryption keys should be stored securely in environment variables
###     - Use HTTPS in production to encrypt data in transit
###     - Regularly rotate encryption keys in production environments

### 11. COMMON IBAN FORMATS
###     - Saudi Arabia: SA + 22 digits (24 characters total)
###     - UAE: AE + 2 check digits + 3 bank code + 16 digits (23 characters)
###     - Kuwait: KW + 2 check digits + 2 bank code + 22 digits (30 characters)
###     - Bahrain: BH + 2 check digits + 4 bank code + 14 alphanumeric (22 characters)

### 12. COMMON SWIFT CODES (Saudi Arabia)
###     - Al Rajhi Bank: ALBISARI
###     - National Commercial Bank: NCBKSAJE
###     - Riyad Bank: RIBLSARI
###     - Saudi British Bank: SABBSARI
###     - Alinma Bank: ALINSARI

### 13. TESTING
###     - Use test JWT tokens for development
###     - Verify encryption by checking database directly (data should be encrypted)
###     - Verify decryption by checking API responses (data should be readable)
###     - Test with invalid UUIDs, missing fields, and unauthorized access

### 14. INTEGRATION NOTES
###     - Bank accounts are linked to users via userId
###     - Deleting a user does not automatically delete bank accounts (consider cascade)
###     - Bank accounts can be used for withdrawal/payout operations
###     - Consider adding verification status for bank accounts in future
